      "message": "Awesome initiative and job Trevor, much appreciated.\nDid a run through of the files and made some suggestions (since they are easier than trying to explain).\nDoing  a thorough code-review would take me a week 😊\n\n\nGenerally:\n* It feels to me like when classes/interfaces/... are generalized`chatgpt` and `gpt` should be replaced with `ai` and not `aichat`.\n\nOther notes (not related to this commit):\n* The source-code could benefit from google-java-format, but that should be done in a follow-up.\n* Should probably not be done in this change (since there are already a bunch of data-classes.) but using `records` instead of data-classes (requires GSon 2.10, don\u0027t know which version Gerrit is using...).",
      "revId": "d8c79db069fb62a80ea8a223ff6bb7bf2197b244",
